    "faq": {
      "type": "ellura-faq-page",
      "blocks": {
        "ellura_faq_page_01": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "About ellura"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_02": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is ellura?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura is a clinically backed supplement that supports urinary tract health* and may help reduce the ability of certain bacteria to adhere to the urinary tract, allowing them to be flushed out naturally¹⁷˒⁶˒¹².</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_03": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the ingredients in ellura?",
            "answer": "<p>Each capsule delivers 36 mg of proanthocyanidins (PACs) from 206 mg of concentrated cranberry fruit juice extract (Gikacran®), the key ingredient clinically backed to support urinary tract health*⁶˒³˒⁷.</p><p>Inactive ingredients: mannitol, magnesium stearate, silicon dioxide and the vegetable shell (hydroxypropylmethylcellulose). They keep the ingredients from sticking together during manufacturing, improve stability and help keep the active PACs bioavailable.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_04": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why does ellura have a new design?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura is the same high-quality supplement — only the packaging has changed. It is now delivered directly from Pharmatoka, its original creators.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_05": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I open the ellura capsules if I have trouble swallowing them?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We recommend mixing the powder into soft food (such as yoghurt or a fruit purée) or a sweet drink such as juice rather than taking it directly, as it has a naturally bitter, astringent taste.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_06": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How ellura works"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_07": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does ellura work?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura harnesses 36 mg of PACs from 100% pure concentrated cranberry fruit juice extract³˒⁴. These soluble, bioactive PACs interact with certain bacteria in a way that may help reduce their ability to adhere to the bladder wall¹⁷˒⁶˒¹². Without the ability to adhere, bacteria are naturally washed out, helping to keep your urinary tract clean*.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_08": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are proanthocyanidins (PACs)?",
            "answer": "<p>PACs are naturally occurring compounds found in cranberry fruit. Research has identified that the A-type PACs in cranberries play a key role in helping support urinary tract health*¹˒².</p><p>ellura is made with a standardised cranberry juice extract produced through an extraction process that preserves these soluble, bioactive PACs, so each capsule delivers 36 mg — the research-based amount to support urinary tract health*.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_09": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is ellura different from other cranberry supplements?",
            "answer": "<p>Not all cranberry supplements are created equal. Many lack the clinically studied 36 mg of soluble, bioactive PACs.</p><p>ellura is made from 100% pure concentrated cranberry fruit juice extract — a high-purity source of soluble A-type PACs shown in research to help reduce the ability of certain bacteria to adhere to the bladder¹⁷˒⁶˒¹². It is standardised using the validated DMAC/A2 method⁹ and backed by 20+ years of research.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_10": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How to take ellura"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_11": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who can benefit from taking ellura?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura provides clinically backed urinary tract support, which may help reduce bacterial adhesion within hours*. Daily use helps maintain urinary tract balance*. Urinary tract health is especially important for women, but men can also benefit. If you have an underlying medical condition, consult your healthcare provider before use.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_12": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How often should I take ellura?",
            "answer": "<p>Take one capsule daily with water, at the same time each day.</p><p>ellura is not intended to treat or cure urinary tract infections; it is clinically backed to support urinary tract health*. Always follow your healthcare professional’s recommendation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_13": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need a prescription?",
            "answer": "<p>No prescription is needed to buy ellura. It has been researched for its role in supporting urinary tract health*³˒² and is recommended by many healthcare professionals. In the US it is marketed as a dietary supplement. <em>[India regulatory category and licence number — to be confirmed]</em></p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_14": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I take ellura with a prescribed antibiotic?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, you can take ellura alongside a prescribed antibiotic to help maintain urinary tract health*¹⁷˒⁶˒³˒¹². ellura is not a substitute for antibiotics, which are necessary to treat an active urinary tract infection.</p><p>Once an infection clears, you can continue taking ellura daily to support urinary tract health. Because long-term antibiotic use for prevention may lead to resistance and unwanted side effects¹³˒⁵, work with your healthcare provider on the best ongoing strategy for you.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_15": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can ellura replace an antibiotic?",
            "answer": "<p>No. If you have a confirmed UTI you will likely need an antibiotic to treat it. See a doctor promptly if you have fever, chills, back or side pain, or blood in your urine.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_16": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Quality"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_17": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is ellura suitable for vegans?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — ellura is encapsulated in a 100% plant-based capsule.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_18": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How is ellura tested for quality?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura is tested at every stage. It is manufactured under Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP) so each batch meets strict standards for purity and potency. The Gikacran® extract complies with USP standards and is free from harmful contaminants¹⁴˒⁸.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_19": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Safety information"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_20": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is ellura acidic?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura has a pH of about 4.44 — mildly acidic, similar to coffee (about 5), soda or tomatoes (4–5). Water is neutral at pH 7; cranberry juice is much more acidic at pH 2.7. ellura contains no caffeine.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_21": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I be allergic to ellura?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura is well tolerated, but if you have a red-fruit allergy check with your healthcare provider first — the active PACs come from cranberry, a red fruit.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_22": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does ellura contain GMOs, artificial ingredients or common allergens?",
            "answer": "<p>No. ellura contains no GMOs, dyes, artificial preservatives, sweeteners, gluten, lactose, corn, dairy, soy, wheat, yeast or added sugars.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_23": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is ellura suitable for children?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura has been used in children for years with no reported side effects. Children under 50 lb (about 23 kg) can take half a capsule daily; 50 lb or more, one capsule daily. The capsule can be opened and mixed into a sweet drink or soft food⁷.</p><p>Please consult your child’s paediatrician before starting ellura.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_24": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is ellura safe during pregnancy or breastfeeding?",
            "answer": "<p>There are no studies on ellura in pregnant or nursing women. Cranberry is generally considered safe, but please consult your healthcare provider before use.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_25": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I take ellura if I have diabetes?",
            "answer": "<p>Please consult your healthcare provider before starting ellura.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_26": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I take ellura if I’m on blood thinners?",
            "answer": "<p>A potential interaction cannot be ruled out. If you take anticoagulant medication, consult your healthcare provider before using ellura.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_27": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are there any side effects?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura is generally very well tolerated and not expected to cause side effects. If you experience any, stop and consult your healthcare provider, and let us know via <a href=\"/pages/contact\">Help &amp; Support</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_28": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can ellura cause kidney stones or worsen existing ones?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura contains low levels of oxalates — only 0.108 mg per capsule, much lower than cranberry juice or whole fruit — which makes it unlikely to cause or worsen kidney stones. If you have a history of kidney stones or severe kidney disease, consult your healthcare provider first.</p>"
          }
        },
        "ellura_faq_page_29": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does ellura help with interstitial cystitis (IC)?",
            "answer": "<p>ellura is not a treatment for interstitial cystitis. If UTIs tend to trigger your IC flares, ellura may help support urinary tract health*. If acidity is a concern, ellura has a pH of about 4.4 and can be taken with an acid reducer. Always consult your healthcare provider for IC management.</p>"
          }
        },
